## Changes

1. Exact-metric definition corrected (definition error, not wording):
   exact = exact gold column list + row multiset + row order ONLY where the
   expected result's `semantic_ordered` contract is true (39/245 main
   queries). Gold-SQL ORDER BY is not the exact metric's ordering contract.
   - paper/stam-m_ja.tex: metric definition (Sec. 3.4), main result (10.6%),
     Table S19 multiaxis caption, Table S20 caption, S8.6 text
   - evaluation/metrics.py docstring; scripts/audit_scoring.py,
     scripts/eval_multiaxis_metrics.py, scripts/derive_main_artifacts.py
     metadata strings; `n_semantic_ordered` added to scoring_audit.json;
     `exact_metric` note re-normalized in multiaxis_results.json /
     main_eval_with_sql.json (deterministic derivation; scores unchanged)
   - The separate `ordered` column in Table S20 is UNCHANGED: it is a
     different metric whose population is gold SQL with ORDER BY (234 main
     queries), value 54.3%. Table S20 caption now states this explicitly.
   - MANIFEST.md: new "ordering contracts" section (39 vs 234).

2. CTE evaluation = 15 queries, all inside main 245:
   - SSOT `dataset.n_cte_queries` 5 -> 15; new keys
     `n_cte_in_ablation_subset` = 5, `n_cte_zero_shot` = 10
   - Sec. 2.1.2 principle (4), Sec. 4.3.2, S8 CTE section, S10 step 3 and
     MANIFEST.md reworded: 5 known/few-shot-covered patterns are in the
     ablation subset; 10 zero-shot patterns are in main 245 but outside the
     ablation subset; the 10 were NOT added from outside the main corpus.
   - Table S21 lower block (ablation conditions) intentionally stays at the
     5 patterns that are in the ablation subset.

3. Variant A (q_proto_*, 20) disclosed as a subset of main 245:
   MANIFEST.md, Sec. 4.3.4 / Table 5 caption, S9.2 — the 100.0% is a
   separate run of the same questions (85.0% within the single main run);
   Variants B/C/D and the untranslated EN-25 are distinct corpora.

4. Main-245 partition table added (Sec. 2.1.2, `tab:main_partition`) and in
   MANIFEST.md; SSOT `dataset.main_partition` (counts, id ranges,
   within-main-run recall of each re-reported subset) and
   `dataset.ordering_contracts` added by paper_scripts/compute_all_figures.py
   with set-relation assertions (ablation/independent/CTE15/proto ⊂ main;
   CTE15 = ablation-CTE ∪ zero-shot-CTE; transfer ∩ main = ∅).

5. Sec. 4.3 opening: one-sentence disclosure that the independent design 100,
   Variant A 20 and CTE 15 (135 main queries) are re-reported as separate
   runs of main-245 subsets, while B/C/D and EN-25 are distinct corpora.

